---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const locale = 'en';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Sales & Customer Operations — Quotations, Invoices, CRM, POS"
  description="Quotations, sales orders, invoices, delivery notes, credit notes, customer management, POS, CRM pipeline, agent commissions, and territory management. Part of Kraal Code ERP."
  locale={locale}
  canonicalUrl="https://kraalcode.com/en/capabilities/sales/"
>
  <section class="page-hero section--warm">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/en/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/en/capabilities/">Capabilities</a></li><li aria-current="page">Sales & Customer Operations</li></ol></nav>
      <h1>Sales & Customer Operations</h1>
      <p class="page-hero-subtext">From first quotation to final receipt. One customer record, one order pipeline, one invoice register — connected to inventory and accounting in real time.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container container--narrow">
    <h2>Who this is for</h2>
    <p>Sales managers, account executives, cashiers, and business owners who need visibility of the entire sales cycle — from quotation to collection. Whether you sell from a counter, through field agents, or via online orders, this module handles the transaction and keeps the ledger current.</p>
    <p>If your business issues invoices, manages a customer base, runs a retail point of sale, or employs field sales agents with commission structures, this module replaces the spreadsheets and disconnected tools with one governed system.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section section--warm"><div class="container">
    <h2>What you can do</h2>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Quotations & Sales Orders</h3><p>Create quotations, convert to sales orders, and generate invoices. Track quotation-to-order conversion rates. Support partial deliveries and backorders.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Customer Invoices</h3><p>Generate invoices with tax calculations, discounts, and multi-currency support. Print or email to customers. Track outstanding balances and payment status.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Delivery Notes</h3><p>Confirm deliveries against sales orders. Stock is deducted automatically on delivery confirmation. Generate delivery note printouts for dispatch.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Customer Management</h3><p>Maintain a customer master with contacts, credit limits, payment terms, price lists, and statement preferences. View customer history, outstanding balances, and transaction ledger.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Point of Sale</h3><p>Touch-optimised POS terminal for retail and hospitality. Supports cash, mobile money, and card payments. Barcode scanning. Multi-terminal per branch. End-of-day cash reconciliation.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Sales CRM</h3><p>Leads and opportunities pipeline. Interaction logging. Contact management. Sales forecasting. Quotation conversion tracking. Performance analytics by rep, territory, and product.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Agent Management</h3><p>Register field sales agents. Assign territories and targets. Track daily sales per agent. Calculate commissions (flat rate, tiered, product-specific). Agents view their own performance through the self-service portal.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Territory Management</h3><p>Define sales territories. Assign agents and customers to territories. Track sales performance by territory. Generate territory-level reports.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container container--narrow">
    <h2>How it connects</h2>
    <p>The sales module sits at the front of the order-to-cash cycle. Every transaction flows downstream automatically:</p>
    <ul class="connection-list">
      <li><strong>Inventory</strong> → stock deducted on delivery confirmation, stock checked on order entry</li>
      <li><strong>Accounting</strong> → revenue and debtor entries posted on invoice approval</li>
      <li><strong>Procurement</strong> → backorders trigger purchase requests</li>
      <li><strong>Sales Agents</strong> → agent stock, commissions, and remittances managed separately</li>
    </ul>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section section--warm"><div class="container container--narrow">
    <h2>Controls and permissions</h2>
    <div class="controls-grid">
      <div class="control-item"><h3>Credit Limits</h3><p>Enforce customer credit limits at order entry. Override requires manager approval. Overdue accounts flagged automatically.</p></div>
      <div class="control-item"><h3>Price Authority</h3><p>Standard price lists with discount bands. Discounts beyond authority require approval. All overrides logged with reason and approver.</p></div>
      <div class="control-item"><h3>Invoice Approval</h3><p>Invoices above configurable thresholds require approval before posting to accounting. Draft invoices can be amended; posted invoices are immutable.</p></div>
      <div class="control-item"><h3>Audit Trail</h3><p>Every quotation, order, invoice, and credit note is logged with user, timestamp, and IP. INSERT-only audit records. No transaction can be silently deleted.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container">
    <h2>See it in action</h2>
    <p class="screenshot-intro">Screenshots from the live Kraal Code system — coming soon.</p>
    <div class="screenshot-grid">
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Point of Sale Terminal</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Invoice Register</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Customer Ledger</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Agent Commissions</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section--dark section"><div class="container text-center">
    <h2>See sales in action</h2>
    <p>Request a demonstration tailored to your sales and customer operations.</p>
    <a href="/en/contact/" class="btn btn--inverse">Request a Demonstration →</a>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding: var(--kc-space-20) 0 var(--kc-space-12);
  }
  .page-hero h1 {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-4xl);
    max-width: 700px;
  }
  .page-hero-subtext {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-lg);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-4);
  }
  .breadcrumb ol {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--kc-space-2);
    font-size: var(--kc-text-sm);
    color: var(--kc-text-tertiary);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-6);
  }
  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--kc-teal);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .breadcrumb li:not(:last-child)::after {
    content: '/';
    margin-left: var(--kc-space-2);
    color: var(--kc-text-tertiary);
  }
  .container--narrow {
    max-width: var(--kc-container-narrow);
  }
  .container--narrow p {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-base);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--kc-leading-relaxed);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-4);
  }
  .feature-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--kc-space-6);
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-8);
  }
  .feature-card {
    padding: var(--kc-space-6);
    background: var(--kc-surface-light);
    border: 1px solid var(--kc-border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--kc-radius-lg);
  }
  .feature-card h3 {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-lg);
    font-family: var(--kc-font-body);
    font-weight: var(--kc-weight-semibold);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-2);
  }
  .feature-card p {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-sm);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
  }
  .connection-list {
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-4);
  }
  .connection-list li {
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-3);
    font-size: var(--kc-text-base);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
  }
  .connection-list strong {
    color: var(--kc-text-primary);
  }
  .controls-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--kc-space-6);
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-6);
  }
  .control-item {
    padding: var(--kc-space-5);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--kc-teal);
  }
  .control-item h3 {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-base);
    font-family: var(--kc-font-body);
    font-weight: var(--kc-weight-semibold);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-1);
  }
  .control-item p {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-sm);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
  }
  .screenshot-intro {
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-6);
  }
  .screenshot-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--kc-space-6);
  }
  .screenshot-placeholder {
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
    background: var(--kc-surface-warm);
    border: 2px dashed var(--kc-border);
    border-radius: var(--kc-radius-lg);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--kc-space-2);
  }
  .screenshot-label {
    font-weight: var(--kc-weight-semibold);
    color: var(--kc-text-primary);
  }
  .screenshot-note {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-sm);
    color: var(--kc-text-tertiary);
  }
  .btn--inverse {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--kc-space-4) var(--kc-space-8);
    font-weight: var(--kc-weight-semibold);
    font-size: var(--kc-text-base);
    border-radius: var(--kc-radius-lg);
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--kc-text-inverse);
    border: 2px solid var(--kc-teal-light);
    transition: all var(--kc-transition-fast);
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-6);
  }
  .btn--inverse:hover {
    background: var(--kc-teal);
    border-color: var(--kc-teal);
  }
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .page-hero h1 {
      font-size: var(--kc-text-3xl);
    }
    .feature-grid,
    .controls-grid,
    .screenshot-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
